{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"“What fabulous fashions we have seen tonight! OOOoooooEEE! I might have to steal a few of those outfits. Now for best story teller. Tell us a story from your past. Enrapture us, transport us.”","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:25:30.302000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867955555652759583","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"Round 2: Best story teller\nTell us a story from your past. Any story. I will roll a d6 to see the crowd’s reaction. You will then roll a d20 and add my roll as your modifier. Advantage can be granted.","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:25:41.330000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867955601907531887","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"\"Finn!\"","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:25:51.102000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867955642894282762","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"Lights go dark and a spring of music, a beat of drums and a low melody turns around the heads of the crowd. So much so they can literally see notes marching in formation.\n\nAmong the marching notes a young child looks up to them, dancing between them. That child is us. Us before the time we faced reality, but stayed in the wonder. As the music picks up that child explores, they adventure to the peaks of towers and delve into the forgotten sewers.\n\nThe notes that March shift and turn to whimsical lights and butterflies. The scene around is a forest by the sea. Fireworks shoot off over it and the child looks back in wonder.\n\nThe child watches ***RED. WHITE. and BLUE*** flash in the sky. The instrumentals swell. \n\nThe flag of the continental union, the United States of America, 13 stars in a circle with red white and blue next to it stands atop the tallest and largest ship over the bay.\n\nThe child's name is hope, and this is our tomorrow that we aim to build, together.\nOne by one we see the notes of butterflies shift into people adjoining hands and standing near with one hand over their hearts","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:26:22.198000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-23T02:26:33.194000Z","id":"867955773320351766","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
