{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Basil","id":"339235123759153162","is_bot":0,"username":"divinedefault"},"author_id":"339235123759153162","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"well it's great to be surrounded by all of these great folks and people.\ntake a moment and relax, sit back and let me tell you of my title as the god of evil.\n\nnow I once was from the circus I was the regular freak,\nI was knife juggler strong man and silver to speak.\n\nthen they ditched me in a dungeon where I met a fair maiden\nan adventurer who took me in with the burdens they were laden\n\ntwas knowledge, and power, and wealth that we sought\nlove and loss was the game and for victory we fought.\n\nthrough ancient ruin we found out secrets divine,\nto help through a planar gate, a dear friend of mine.\nand once he was home we had thought we were fine.\n\nbetrayed, murdered, a friend by a friend,\na deck of cards to kill and make an end.\nand our will was not broken, but met with a bend.\n\na new deck we sought, not of many things but of good\nto bring back the friend as we should.\n\ntwo dragons we fought, both silvers and red\nthe silver a trickster who'd trick us dead.\nwith riddles and valor here is what was said\n\n\"to make right the death done unto us we seek out these cards\nyou've seen the might of our sorcerer and the cunning of our bard.\"\n\nour friend we took back from the clutches of beyond\nand godhood we sought to and heaven we'd abscond.\n\nface the trials we did, my sister and I\nthe goddess of good to my evil, unto the time I die","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:39:07.450000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867958983019876442","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
